<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scaurĭānus</span></b> , a,
		um, v. 2. Scaurus.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			† <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scaurus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαῦρος</span> [cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαιός</span>],
				<i>with large and swollen ankles</i>, <i>having the ankles bunching out</i> (cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">varus, valgus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 45, 105, § 254</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illum Balbutit scaurum pravis fultum male
					talis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 3, 48</span></i>
			.</div>
